IMPORT prelude

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 4: regulation 13 (minimum number of qualifying years).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- A "qualifying year" is a tax year that counts towards the state pension; it is
-- defined by section 2(4) of the Pensions Act 2014, which is not among the inputs,
-- so the number of qualifying years a person has is a plain input here.
-- The number of qualifying years for the FULL rate is set by the 2014 Act (not by
-- these Regulations), so for the full rate the answer is "not covered".

§ `Part 4: Minimum Qualifying Period`

DECLARE KindOfStatePension IS ONE OF
    `a state pension at the reduced rate`
    `a state pension at the transitional rate`
    `a state pension at the full rate`

DECLARE EnoughYears IS ONE OF
    `the person has enough qualifying years`
    `the person does not have enough qualifying years`
    `these Regulations do not set the number of qualifying years for this rate`

§§ `Regulation 13(1): the reduced rate`

-- Gloss: to get a state pension at the reduced rate (a part of the full rate) a person
-- needs at least ten qualifying years. The purposes named are section 2(3) of the
-- 2014 Act.
-- src:142 | (1) For the purposes of section 2(3) of the 2014 Act (entitlement to state pension at full or reduced rate), the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the reduced rate is ten.
@ref Regulation 13(1) (src:142)
`regulation 13(1): the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension at the reduced rate` MEANS 10

§§ `Regulation 13(2): the transitional rate`

-- Gloss: the transitional rate is the rate for people with years before 6 April 2016
-- (section 4 of the 2014 Act); it too needs at least ten qualifying years.
-- src:143 | (2) For the purposes of section 4(2) of the 2014 Act (entitlement to a state pension at transitional rate), the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the transitional rate is ten.
@ref Regulation 13(2) (src:143)
`regulation 13(2): the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension at the transitional rate` MEANS 10

§§ `Regulation 13: does the person have the minimum?`

-- src:142 | (1) For the purposes of section 2(3) of the 2014 Act (entitlement to state pension at full or reduced rate), the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the reduced rate is ten.
-- src:143 | (2) For the purposes of section 4(2) of the 2014 Act (entitlement to a state pension at transitional rate), the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension payable at the transitional rate is ten.
@ref Regulation 13(1) and (2) (src:142-143)
GIVEN kind IS A KindOfStatePension
      `the number of qualifying years the person has` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A EnoughYears
`regulation 13: whether the person has the minimum number of qualifying years` kind `the number of qualifying years the person has` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a state pension at the reduced rate` THEN
        IF `the number of qualifying years the person has` AT LEAST `regulation 13(1): the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension at the reduced rate`
        THEN `the person has enough qualifying years`
        ELSE `the person does not have enough qualifying years`
    WHEN `a state pension at the transitional rate` THEN
        IF `the number of qualifying years the person has` AT LEAST `regulation 13(2): the minimum number of qualifying years for a state pension at the transitional rate`
        THEN `the person has enough qualifying years`
        ELSE `the person does not have enough qualifying years`
    WHEN `a state pension at the full rate` THEN `these Regulations do not set the number of qualifying years for this rate`
